<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Iterated round-trip translation examples.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Tables <a href="#A4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Iterated round-trip translation examples. ‣ Appendix D Additional Results ‣ Markovian Generation Chains in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and <a href="#A4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Iterated round-trip translation examples. ‣ Appendix D Additional Results ‣ Markovian Generation Chains in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> provide illustrative round-trip translation chains (EN<math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math>French<math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math>EN), highlighting early stabilization and occasional alternation between near-identical variants.</p>
</div>
